WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:05.280
Since 2001, the Fast and Furious movies have
morphed into a massive, sprawling franchise.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:10.820
In fact, the series easily rivals most comic
book movies for surprisingly dense lore, outrageous

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:14.200
action, and heroic (one might even say superheroic)
leads.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:19.039
In 2001's The Fast and the Furious, we're
introduced to Brian O'Connor, an undercover

00:00:19.039 --> 00:00:23.440
cop tasked with taking down a gang of muscle-car-loving
thieves who have been stealing what they claim

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.460
to be millions of dollars of DVD players.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:29.060
Brian finds a possible lead in Dominic Toretto, the charismatic ringleader

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:32.920
of a group of car heads who may or may not
be the same gang that Brian's after.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.380
"I live my life a quarter-mile at a time."

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:42.100
To make things even more complicated, Dom's
sister Mia, the shop owner of Toretto's Market,

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.840
is the object of Brian's affection.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.620
Brian impresses Dom with his driving, eventually
ingratiating himself into Dom's team, which

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:50.200
isn't a family just yet.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:54.600
Unfortunately, Brian soon learns that he can
only play both sides of the law for so long,

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:58.090
and comes clean to the Toretto family when
it looks like Dom and his gang will end up

00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:59.780
on the wrong end of a trucker's shotgun.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.940
With Brian's cover blown and Dom forced to
leave town, the two have one last quarter-mile

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:04.440
race.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:08.360
Ultimately, rather than take his new friend
into custody, Brian gives Dom the keys to

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.580
his car and lets him race off into the distance.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.740
2 Fast 2 Furious surprisingly isn't the second
part of this franchise.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:19.610
Instead, that honor goes to The Turbo Charged
Prelude for 2 Fast 2 Furious, a short film

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:22.180
which sees Brian on the run after letting
Dom go free.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:26.380
For some reason, this leads to a nationwide
manhunt, with his face plastered all over

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:27.200
the nightly news.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:30.840
That sort of thing tends to present a problem
when you're driving across America winning

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:34.400
street races like some sort of gear shaft
version of Johnny Appleseed.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:37.920
When cops seize his vehicle while Brian's
driving through Texas, he's able to hitch

00:01:37.921 --> 00:01:42.270
a ride with an unnamed woman who recognizes
his face, possibly because of his uncanny

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:44.799
resemblance to Lance Harbor from Varsity Blues.

00:01:44.799 --> 00:01:49.610
After that, he buys a new car, wins more street
races, and finds himself in Miami, the city

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:50.600
where the heat is on.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:56.540
In 2003's 2 Fast 2 Furious, Brian has fully
transformed from undercover cop with an unmistakable

00:01:56.540 --> 00:02:01.770
surfer accent into a king of the Miami street
racing scene with an unmistakable surfer accent.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:06.420
Together with organizer and former racer Tej,
Brian's been racking up the bills and notoriety

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:06.920
in Miami.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.020
That all comes to a screeching halt when he's
arrested by the Miami Police after they fire

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.780
an electronic harpoon into his car.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:16.880
The police want Brian to go undercover inside
a criminal organization, and they're willing

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:21.380
to wipe Brian's criminal record if he can
take down Verone, Miami's resident drug lord.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:25.380
Brian recruits his childhood best friend and
ex-con Roman to help him race his way into

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.540
Verone's good graces.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:30.420
With the help of another undercover agent,
Monica Fuentes, Brian and Roman

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:35.040
capture Verone, clear their criminal records,
and walk away with a pile of illicitly acquired

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:35.540
cash.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:39.040
And that's about when the timeline hits turbo
speed with chronological hijinx.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.891
Los Bandoleros was a short film co-written
and directed by Vin Diesel that serves as

00:02:43.891 --> 00:02:48.349
a prelude to the fourth film, Fast &amp; Furious,
following Dom as he assembles a new crew for

00:02:48.349 --> 00:02:51.380
an upcoming heist of a gasoline truck in the
Dominican Republic.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:55.380
Letty's back to rekindle her romance with
Dom, but she's not the only familiar face

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:56.180
in the short film.

00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:00.220
Han originally appeared and died three years
earlier in The Fast and the Furious: Tokyo

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:02.540
Drift, which was the third movie released.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:06.910
A quick line of dialogue establishes that
the Han we see here has never been to Japan,

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.980
so we know that this takes place before Tokyo
Drift.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:12.940
For now, though, all you need to know is that
Dom loves Letty, the people of the Dominican

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:15.920
Republic, and stealing gas from the rich to
give to the poor.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:21.040
2009's Fast &amp; Furious begins with the heist
planned in the Los Bandoleros short.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.230
Dom, Letty, Han, Tego, and Santos steal a
bunch of gas to give to the people of the

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:29.250
Dominican Republic, but their celebration
is short-lived; Dom knows that as long as

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:33.410
he's a wanted criminal, Letty's in danger
of being arrested too, so he leaves Letty

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:37.180
in the middle of the night, off to go live
his life one quarter-mile at a time.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:41.360
Meanwhile, Brian is working with the FBI as
a field agent, trying to find leads on a drug

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.500
lord named Braga.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.640
Dom is forced to return to Los Angeles after
learning that Letty was seemingly killed by

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:50.560
one of Braga's men while she was working with
Brian to take the drug lord down in exchange

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:52.080
for clearing Dom's criminal record.

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:56.340
Dom and Brian both go undercover in Braga's
street-racing organization Brian intending

00:03:56.349 --> 00:03:58.630
to catch Braga, Dom intending to kill him.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:02.920
While there, they run into and befriend Gisele,
Braga's wondrous right-hand woman.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:05.900
Eventually, Dom and Brian reconcile and take
Braga down.

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:08.560
"I woulda won that race if you didn't cheat."

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:13.200
"You hit your head hard."

00:04:14.989 --> 00:04:19.500
Unfortunately, Dom is captured by the FBI
and sentenced to 25 years in prison for all

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.500
of his prior street-racing related crimes.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.960
Luckily for him, Brian is used to going against
the law to save his friend.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:29.100
The film ends with Brian, Mia, and the rest
of the crew teaming up to break Dom out.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:33.240
2011's Fast Five picks up immediately where
Fast &amp; Furious left off.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:37.220
Dom escapes from prison with his family, and
the crew heads to Rio de Janeiro to figure

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:38.260
out their next moves.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:42.500
Brian takes a gig stealing cars from a train,
but unbeknownst to the Family, one of the

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:46.530
cars they steal belongs to Reyes [RAY-ez],
a ruthless drug lord who controls Rio with

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:47.420
an iron fist.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:51.750
Dom, Mia, and Brian recognize that they've
got a golden opportunity to steal enough money

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:54.340
from Reyes to fund their fugitive
lives permanently.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:59.070
It's more than a three-person job, so they
put out the call for the whole Family to assemble:

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:04.940
Roman, Tej, Giselle, Han, Tego, and Santos
all arrive ready to steal 100 million from

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:05.440
Reyes.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:08.220
Unfortunately, Reyes isn't the only obstacle
in their way.

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:12.580
Luke Hobbs, a Diplomatic Security Service
agent and all-around tough guy, is on the

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:13.500
hunt for the Family.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:17.630
Along for the ride is Elena, a Rio patrol
officer with a grudge against Reyes for the

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:18.620
murder of her husband.

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:21.000
Dom and Hobbs have their requisite tough-guy
face-off…

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:23.200
"This… is BRAZIL!"

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:29.460
...but they're forced to work together after
Reyes kills Hobbs' entire team, save for himself

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:30.460
and Elena.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:35.180
The Family's heist goes off without a hitch,
and Hobbs gives Dom a full 24-hour grace period

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:37.860
before they resume their muscular-cat-and-muscular-mouse
chase.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:41.620
After the end of Fast Five, there were only
two things that could get the Family back

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:45.070
in action: the promise of amnesty and the
knowledge that Letty is alive.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:49.240
It turns out that Letty survived the explosion
back in Fast &amp; Furious, but got amnesia.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:53.720
She was then conscripted into a kind of evil
version of the Fast Family led by the villainous

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:54.380
Owen Shaw.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:58.360
Hobbs and his new partner Riley bring the
Fast Family, because obviously, only fast

00:05:58.360 --> 00:05:59.940
thieves can catch fast thieves.

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:03.860
"Wasn't that hard to find you, Toretto."

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:07.620
"Wasn't hiding."

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:12.120
Eventually, through the magic of street racing,
Dom's able to convince Letty that she's being

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:15.120
manipulated by Shaw, and convinces her to
join the team.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:19.580
Unfortunately, she's not the only double agent;
Riley's been working for Shaw the whole time,

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:22.160
just waiting for the perfect opportunity to
betray Hobbs.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:26.150
It all comes to a head on the world's longest
airstrip as the Fast Family battles to stop

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:28.940
Shaw from escaping with secret government
technology.

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:33.880
Gisele sacrifices herself to save Han, Shaw
is stopped, and ultimately, the Family's previous

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:37.360
crimes are forgiven, allowing them to return
to Los Angeles once again.

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:43.240
After Giselle's death in 2013's Fast &amp; Furious
6, Han finally makes good on his promise to

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:47.760
visit Tokyo in a movie released seven years
earlier: The Fast and the Furious: Tokyo Drift.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:51.979
The third movie released in the series, Tokyo
Drift was a failed effort to reinvent the

00:06:51.979 --> 00:06:56.460
franchise without Paul Walker or Vin Diesel,
and most of the film concerns itself with

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:57.260
Sean Boswell.

00:06:57.340 --> 00:07:01.900
He's a high schooler sent to live with his
father in Tokyo after his penchant for street

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:03.840
racing lands him in hot water in the states.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:08.310
Sean meets Han, whose cool-as-ice persona
and street racing skills have made him a major

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:10.080
player in the underground racing scene.

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:14.140
Han takes Sean under his wing, even loaning
him a car and tutoring him in the ways of

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:17.300
drifting to beat D.K., the nephew of a Yakuza
crime boss.

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:20.780
“You know what D.K. stands for?"

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:23.380
"Donkey Kong?"

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:25.220
"Drift King."

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:30.660
Unfortunately, Han's training is interrupted
when D.K. and his uncle's henchmen attack

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:31.160
Han's garage.

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:35.700
In the ensuing chase scene, Han is tragically
hit by a passing motorist, and his fuel tank

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:37.480
goes up in a massive ball of fire.

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:41.790
Consumed with racing vengeance, Sean challenges
D.K. to a race in which the winner has to

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:42.760
leave town forever.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:47.500
Sean wins, becoming the new Drift King, and
Dom shows up, explaining that Han was "family."

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:52.340
The post-credits scene of Fast &amp; Furious 6
returned to Han's death in Tokyo Drift, but

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:56.530
with one major bit of context: a mysterious
stranger who's following the chase on a police

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:57.020
scanner.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:01.400
With careful timing, the stranger speeds right
into Han, and then the as yet unnamed character

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:05.480
calls Dom on the phone as Han's car burns,
delivering a foreboding message:

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:13.199
"Dominic Toretto, you don't know me… but
you're about to."

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:18.580
There's nothing more important than family
in the Fast &amp; Furious universe, but bad guys

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:19.460
have families, too.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:22.220
In this case, Owen Shaw has a big brother
named Deckard.

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:25.320
He kills Han in the post-credits scene of
Fast &amp; Furious 6.

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:29.910
When the Family hears about Han's death, Dom
travels to Tokyo to pay his respects and start

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:30.880
the hunt for Deckard.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:35.079
Meanwhile, Deckard's been busy; he's already
attacked Hobbs and Elena to find out everything

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:36.500
he can about the Fast Family.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:40.959
When Dom finally meets Deckard, their climatic
street fight is interrupted by a mysterious

00:08:40.959 --> 00:08:45.329
government agent named Mr. Nobody, who needs
Dom and his team to do some odd jobs for them

00:08:45.329 --> 00:08:49.940
in return for the use of God's Eye, a hacking
tool that can find anyone on the planet, including

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:50.440
Deckard.

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:55.260
"This time, it ain't just about being fast."

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:01.860
The team rescues Ramsey, the hacker who designed
God's Eye, from a Somali mercenary trying

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:03.900
to use the device for nefarious reasons.

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:07.420
It all comes to a head in Los Angeles, of
course, where Dom and his team need to keep

00:09:07.429 --> 00:09:10.989
Ramsey away from Deckard long enough for her
to disable the God's Eye.

00:09:10.989 --> 00:09:12.680
Fortunately, they have some help from Hobbs.

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:14.200
"Daddy's gotta go to work."

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:24.579
Deckard Shaw is taken to jail after Dom beats
him by stomping on a parking garage like the

00:09:24.579 --> 00:09:28.750
Incredible Hulk, and then Dom briefly dies
and is resurrected with the power of love,

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:29.640
thus avenging Han.

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:33.990
The real-life death of Paul Walker leads to
the character Brian's retirement, as he rides

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:35.920
off into the sunset with Mia and their son.

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:41.040
After going to Havana and winning a street
race by driving backwards in a car that literally

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:45.819
explodes, Dom runs into Cipher, a cyberterrorist
who blackmails him into betraying his Family

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:48.240
for the only reason he would: even more family.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:52.720
Dom's ex-girlfriend Elena secretly had his
child between the events of Fast &amp; Furious

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:57.369
6 and Fate of the Furious, and Cipher is holding
the two of them hostage unless Dom gives her

00:09:57.369 --> 00:09:59.160
what she wants: nuclear weapons.

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:03.600
While Dom battles against his Family and Mr.
Nobody, he calls in favors from some old friends

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:07.560
and recent enemies, including the Shaw Brothers,
who now have full-on jetpacks.

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:12.180
They all help Dom double-cross Cipher, but
unfortunately, Elena dies, and Cipher escapes

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:14.369
to lick her wounds and plot a future sequel.

00:10:14.369 --> 00:10:18.879
Deckard Shaw arrives to the requisite post-battle
meal with Dom's son, who's named Brian after

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:19.680
Dom's best friend.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:21.240
What's next for the Family?

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:25.819
Coming in August of 2019 is Fast &amp; Furious
Presents: Hobbs and Shaw, which will see the

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:29.220
eponymous odd couple facing off against a
super-powered Idris Elba.

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:31.220
"Look at me.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:33.820
I'm black Superman."

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:38.959
Fast &amp; Furious 9 is slated for 2020, and while
there hasn't been much news about it since,

00:10:38.959 --> 00:10:43.440
an animated show called Fast &amp; Furious: Spy
Racers was announced in April 2018.

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:48.079
Now, with reports of on-set conflict between
series leads, the future looks cloudy.

00:10:48.079 --> 00:10:51.550
The spinoff might be a way to keep Dwayne
"The Rock" Johnson and his popular character

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:54.500
in the universe without him sharing screen
time with Vin Diesel.

00:10:54.769 --> 00:10:57.220
Whatever else is on the road ahead, no one
really knows for sure.

00:10:57.220 --> 00:11:00.660
All we can do is get there ourselves, one
quarter-mile at time.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:03.280
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:06.660
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies are coming soon.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:10.680
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

